## D. PROCESS (ROOT's assessment for Ember)
- Throughput shape: 6–8 landers on a serial CAS cost 3–5 full judges (~25 min each) per landing (measured first day:
  6 of 13 landers hit the age bound; ties chain). GATES-20 cuts a re-base to ~58% of a judge; GATES-21 (merge
  train) is the structural fix. ROOT RECOMMENDS: switch NOW to BATCH INTEGRATION: an INTEGRATOR lane assembles
  N lanes' patches onto main, runs ONE judge, lands, bisects on red; lanes hand patches (they already do for
  flag days) instead of each running scripts/commit. Every landed tree is still judged; the judge count falls ~4×.
- Context turnover: a lane lives ~350–450K tokens ≈ one big landing; handoffs cost an hour each and lose the
  finding that did not make the file (the collision vacuity crossed layers a day late).
- Re-verification: standing runs every row after every landing (GATES' duty) and vacuity readers read every
  theorem with the disjunct check; there is NO periodic whole-tree re-read by ROOT beyond that, and standing is
  RED right now (warm/cold), which hides everything behind it until 20d lands.

