## 3. DROPPED PROMISES

**Method.** `cv deferrals <id> --open-tasks --json` over the three roots (b3795e84, ce776c01, c1e4d723), 20 major b3795e84/ce776c01 lanes (INTEGRATOR 1–4, TURN-LOG 1–4, FLOORS 1–2, CONSENT-MODEL 1–3, CODEC-SHAPES, STATE-AT-3, PERF-MEMO, PERF-FIX-4, PERF-CLIENT-2, HP-1b, CENSUS-REVIEW, MERGE-KEEPER-2, DEPUTY-KERNEL, DEPUTY-PLATFORM), and four ~/dev/minidregg sessions (905fe751, 4a22422c, 35f3668a, d0d33f7b). Each candidate was then checked against the task store (`cv task list --tsv --since 2026-10-01`, 485 open/claimed), `git log origin/main --grep`, and GitHub (`gh pr/issue view`).

**Counts.** 697 deferral phrases scanned. cv marked 290 MATCHED and 407 UNMATCHED. The MATCHED count is too high: cv calls it a match when the two texts share three words, and spot checks show many false matches. b3795e84#7 "re-arm the 20 dead plants" matched PRIVATE-TRANSFER-DEAD. b3795e84#1543 "Hermes AppArmor, your call" matched NODE-INIT-86. Of the 407 UNMATCHED, most are noise: "queued behind a slot", "nothing to route", or "when train Cn lands" from fn's train cadence. **About 20 still matter**, listed below. One more scope note: the lanes record their open items in work/*-LOG.md continuation files rather than in transcript phrases, so the lanes themselves yielded few deferrals. The lane continuation items are summarised in the last subsection.

