| D3 | carry `rejoin`: trust on first use, by design | a checked join to a carried World | a sponsor signs an invitation pinning the carried base; the joiner adopts thin | PROTOCOL + KERNEL | 1 lane-day | off |
| D4 | founder nonce "on its word"; compare `input HEX` out of band | a founder that checks its own World | founder genesis from inputs the founder made or signed | PROTOCOL, OPS | hours–1 lane-day | off |
| D5 | `forgotten` row's literal 110 / 3100 heights | heights derived from `Bounds.windowMax` | compute them from `windowMax` / `journalForgets` | PROTOCOL | hours | off |
| D6 | `Follow.loop` plant uses `runRooted` as the follower's admission; the CLI loop "read off, not run at more than 64 Turns" | the follow CLI loop at scale | covered by C1 (bar.sh runs `host follow` per member) plus a deployed-param follow plant | HOST | in C1 | on (via C1) |
| D7 | true-by-construction or read-off claims a reader cannot refute | theorems or gates | one gate or plant each (list below) | KERNEL, HOST, PROTOCOL | hours each | off |
| D8 | ed25519-dalek signs (trusted, unverified) | Lean's `Ed25519.sign` | bytes-equality against Lean's sign per call, or sign through the FFI | CLIENT | 1 lane-day | off |
| D9 | kernel-sim's two-law stub program | LANG's program under the generator | keep; it is an instrument (LANG's program runs in rows and lang-journey) | — | — | off |
| E1–E12 | fixtures and controls | — | see §5: keep, replace or delete each | various | — | mixed |
| F1–F12 | deferred by trigger | — | see §6: trigger and whether it has fired | various | — | mixed |

