# Exit codes of a nanodregg unit

A unit runs `nd-supervise … -- host …`. nd-supervise passes the child's code through, so one
code space holds both tables: `host` (Host.Status, below 64) and nd-supervise's own
(Protocol.SupervisorExit, 64 and up). `host` prints `refused NAME` or `exit NAME` on stderr.

## host

| code | name | class | systemd | operator |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | eof | done | stays stopped (success) | nothing: the supervisor closed the stream |
| 3 | uncertain | restart | restarted after 2 s; failed past 5 starts in 120 s | automatic; replies were `uncertain`, clients look their calls up |
| 4 | fuel | restart | restarted after 2 s; failed past 5 starts in 120 s | never an exit: a fuel round reopens in process (D4); seen from outside, a defect: report to HOST |
| 5 | sealIo | restart | restarted after 2 s; failed past 5 starts in 120 s | automatic; check the disk's space and errors |
| 6 | ioServing | restart | restarted after 2 s; failed past 5 starts in 120 s | automatic; an IO error after the open: check the disk |
| 8 | usage | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | fix the unit's argv |
| 9 | entropy | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | the OS random source failed: do not genesis on this box |
| 10 | recordTooLarge | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | a defect or the HOST-14 design limit: report to HOST |
| 11 | worldTooLarge | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | a defect: the World would encode past worldBytesMax (HOST-57, a bound derived from the budget), which no World this binary's budget admits can reach by admitted turns; keep the Store untouched, report to HOST |
| 12 | indexTooLarge | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | a defect or the HOST-14 design limit: report to HOST |
| 13 | io | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | the STORE path or the IN file is absent, a Store file is unreadable (EACCES, EIO), or a file was removed between the open's check and its open: check the path and permissions (the call and errno are on stderr) |
| 16 | locked | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | another writer holds the Store: find its unit; never start a second |
| 17 | exists | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | genesis into an existing Store: choose another path |
| 18 | badKey | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | `STORE/key` is not 32 bytes: restore it from the backup |
| 19 | shortRead | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | a file changed under the open: stop every writer, then `host check` |
| 20 | missing | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | a Store file (key, a segment file `seg.<o>.log`, the index file `index.<k0>.log`, or base.world; stderr names the missing file) is absent from an existing STORE directory: never re-create it or genesis over it; restore the Store's files together from one backup (RUNBOOK §5); a directory left by a genesis that crashed part way is moved aside by hand, never deleted by a unit; if STORE names a directory that holds no Store at all, check the path |
| 21 | baseTooLarge | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | the Store is damaged or not a Store: restore (RUNBOOK §5) |
| 22 | baseCorrupt | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | the Store is damaged or not a Store: restore (RUNBOOK §5) |
| 23 | baseUndecodable | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | the Store is damaged or not a Store: restore (RUNBOOK §5) |
| 24 | segmentShort | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | the Store is damaged or not a Store: restore (RUNBOOK §5) |
| 25 | tailTooLong | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | the Store is damaged or not a Store: restore (RUNBOOK §5) |
| 26 | corrupt | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | bad bytes with a verifying frame after them (the history `host check` reads: a kept segment file from its header on, the origin frame at 0 when it is kept), or corrupt history before the base: restore (RUNBOOK §5) |
| 27 | record | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | a record does not fold: a defect, report to HOST and KERNEL |
| 28 | tagWidth | fatal | stopped (RestartPreventExitStatus) | a broken sealer: a defect, report to HOST |
