### launcher/src/bin/grain-launch.rs
1: //! `grain-launch ROOT BROKER MEMBER LABEL PIDS CONTROLLER [ARG...]`
2: //!
3: //! Starts CONTROLLER (the Lean `hosting-controller`, or the test's `hosting-drive`) confined, with
4: //! read access to `ROOT/worlds/LABEL/store` only, and two pipes: it reads action frames from the
5: //! controller's stdout and writes report frames to its stdin. Each launch is one
6: //! `nanodregg_sandbox::command` over the frame's plan joined onto ROOT, its `broker` sockets onto
7: //! BROKER (keybroker's socket root, HOSTING-17) and its `member` sockets onto MEMBER (where nd serves
8: //! each resident's member socket, HOSTING-20/25). The three roots must be pairwise disjoint trees,
9: //! or the launcher ends `rootsOverlap` before it starts anything. A launch naming a path that is not
10: //! its own grain's (a program, read, write or exec path outside `worlds/LABEL/grains/<grain>/`, or a
11: //! socket of either root other than `<grain>/<name>`) ends the run `foreignPath` (a defect in the
12: //! controller: another grain's socket is another grain's identity). Every child's argv is its plan's
13: //! paths as joined, field for field (`plan_argv`, HOSTING-27). Each child gets a PID file
14: //! `PIDS/<grain>.pid`, removed when the child is reaped. A kill stops the child by its own handle
15: //! (the PID in that file). When the controller's pipe closes, every child is killed and reaped,
16: //! then the launcher exits with a name on stderr. While idle it reports its clock (`tick`, every
17: //! `TICK_MS`, HOSTING-38). It decides nothing: a frame it cannot decode, or
18: //! a frame that breaks a law, ends the run by name.
