1: //! `nd-members MEMBER MEMBERS STATE FOLLOW PIDS HOST_SOCK PEER SUPERVISE ND HOST STORE [--hide PATH]…
2: //! -- /ABS/DECIDER [ARG]…`
3: //!
4: //! Each resident's member socket, for exactly the resident grains the World holds (HOSTING-30,
5: //! CLIENT-29). It asks its decider `residents` at start and every `TICK` (the frames keybroker reads,
6: //! `residents::ask`). For each name answered whose member is provisioned it runs two existing
7: //! `nd-supervise` children, which bind, check peers, bound fds and name every close exactly as
8: //! nd-supervise does:
9: //! - the resident's own follower (a follower is ONE member's command machine: every call and
10: //!   envelope it plans names its MEMBER, so it is never shared), `FOLLOW/<name>/follow.sock` →
11: //!   `host follow STATE/<name>/store MEMBER GRANT`, MEMBER and GRANT read from the provisioning
12: //!   step's `STATE/<name>/follow` (`HEX HEX` and LF, 0600, chain-checked), confined to write that
13: //!   Store, with MEMBERS hidden;
14: //! - once that follower answers a command (after all its startup checks), `MEMBER/<name>/nd.sock` → `nd --stdio MEMBERS/<name>
15: //!   FOLLOW/<name>/follow.sock HOST_SOCK`, confined to write the workspace and connect [HOST_SOCK,
16: //!   its own follow socket] (CLIENT-24), with STATE hidden: it reads the World only through the
17: //!   follow socket and can neither write nor read a follower Store or a `follow` file (HOSTING-32,
18: //!   cv 01a1507c-7245; `Hosting.Proofs.Plan.roots_disjoint`: MEMBERS and STATE are disjoint trees).
19: //!   The socket is 0660 for uid PEER in MEMBER's group (`--group --peer`), or 0600 when PEER is
20: //!   this uid (HOSTING-21).
21: //!
22: //! Each child hides STORE and every `--hide` path; each has a PID file in PIDS. A child that ends is
23: //! started again at most every `RESTART_AFTER`; past `STARTS_MAX` starts in `STARTS_WINDOW` the name
24: //! is `memberCrashLoop`, left unbound until the answer changes. A member not yet provisioned is
25: //! retried every tick and named once (`memberMissing`), so provisioning just after the birth
26: //! binds it within a tick. A name no longer answered loses both sockets, both directories and both
27: //! children, each SIGTERMed to name every peer's close (CLIENT-30), reaped on later ticks, SIGKILLed
28: //! past `GRACE`, counted until gone; a rebirth of its name waits. A resident's own trouble is a name
29: //! on stderr and that resident unbound, never an end (`memberMissing`, `socketDirShared`,
30: //! `memberCrashLoop`, `memberSpawn`, `memberStopping`, `memberStopForced`): one resident must not stop the others.
31: //! Its own ends are `members_exit` (Lean's `Hosting.MembersExit`); the decider's own end is passed
32: //! through, and a World past `RESIDENTS_MAX` ends it with the decider's code for that fact (7).
