### launcher/src/bin/probe.rs
1: //! The launcher tests' grain (`launcher/tests/isolation.rs`, `launcher/tests/resident.rs`). Run as
2: //! `<grain>/pkg/probe`, with no arguments and an empty environment (the sandbox clears both), it
3: //! reads `probe.targets` beside itself (lines `NAME OP PATH`), tries each in order, and appends one
4: //! line per target to `<grain>/vol/probe.out` as soon as it is tried, so a test can follow it:
5: //! `NAME ok` (a `list` prints `ok` and the sorted names, comma-separated) or `NAME denied <errno
6: //! name>`. The ops:
7: //! - `read`, `write`, `list`: the file system;
8: //! - `connect`: open a unix socket (a resident's broker socket, HOSTING-17);
9: //! - `ask`: connect to a broker socket and send one ask (model `claude-m`, 10 tokens, `hello`),
10: //!   then print `ok reply <text>` (the reply text the Lean decider read, HOSTING-29), `ok status
11: //!   <status>` or `ok refused <broker refusal>`. Every byte received is
12: //!   appended to `<grain>/vol/probe.recv`, so the test can check that no key reached the grain;
13: //! - `wait`: wait (at most `WAIT`) until the file PATH exists, so a test can sequence the grain
14: //!   with what it does outside (`ok`, or `denied timeout`);
15: //! - `nd`: `NAME nd SOCK WORD...`: connect to a member socket (`nd --stdio` behind nd-supervise,
16: //!   HOSTING-20) and send the WORDs as one command (the mux child wire, the client's own frame
17: //!   and layout code), then print `ok <exit> <stdout>` (or `<stderr>` when the exit is not OK),
18: //!   newlines as `|`.
19: //!
20: //! It finds itself by argv[0] (no /proc under bwrap). Exit 3 when it cannot write its own volume.
21: //!
22: //! Run in `nd`'s place by nd-members (`launcher/tests/members.rs`, HOSTING-32) it is started as
23: //! `probe --stdio WS FOLLOW_SOCK HOST_SOCK`: then its directory is the member workspace WS, the one
24: //! path that child may write: `WS/probe.targets` in, `WS/probe.out` out, so a test reads what nd's
25: //! own confinement lets it touch.
26: 
